   "id": "yevamot.40a.16",
   "daf": "40a",
   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "אִם יֵשׁ שָׁם אָב. דְּאָמַר מָר: אָב קוֹדֵם לְכׇל יוֹצְאֵי יְרֵכוֹ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states: «If there is a father» of the deceased, who is still alive, the property of the deceased belongs to the father. The Gemara explains: «As the Master said» with regard to the laws of inheritance (Bava Batra 115a): «A father» of the deceased «takes precedence over all» the father’s «descendants.» Therefore, since the father is still alive, the brothers do not inherit at all."
  }
 ],
